          "line": 75,
          "message": "The signing certificate does not use the separately declared signing key. Link the certificate to that key so its public key can verify signatures made by the release identity.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The certificate resource generates its own backing key from its certificate policy, while release_signing_key grants the release identity Crypto User access to the separate azurerm_key_vault_key.signing resource.",
            "failureScenario": "When the release workflow signs an image digest with azurerm_key_vault_key.signing, verification with the public key from azurerm_key_vault_certificate.signing fails because the certificate was created with a different key. This defeats the signing and verification flow and risks accepting or rejecting images incorrectly (OWASP A08:2025 Software and Data Integrity Failures)."
          }
        }
